## Repo layout (single Next app at root)

Product code lives at repo root — not under `apps/studio`.

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `app/` | Next.js routes (thin; compose features) |
| `features/` | Operator jobs (`<entity>-<objective>/`) + `studio-shell` chrome |
| `data/` | `data/gates/` + `data/<Entity>/{dto,dpo,dal}` |
| `domain/` | Business rules, Build, AI contracts — no UI |
| `services/` | Processors, env, `services/db` pool |
| `drizzle/` | Schema + migrations |
| `utilities/` | Root shared pure helpers |
| `stores/` | Client stores |
| `renderers/` | Shared render helpers |

In-repo pnpm workspaces: `packages/plugins/*`, `packages/libraries/*` only.

`@eden-ecommerce/design` and `@eden-ecommerce/lib` are **exact GitHub Packages semver pins** in root `package.json` — not workspace members, not gitignored clones. Work in those repos, publish, bump pin here.

Storybook lives in **`eden-ecommerce/design`** repo — not this tree.

**Not applicable here:** React Native / generic mobile structure guides (`navigation/`, `themes/`, `components/`, `locales/`, `assets/`, `utils/` as app layers). Routing is `app/`; UI comes from `@eden-ecommerce/design`.

**Not used:** `workflows/`, `'use workflow'`, `domain/plugins`, `domain/pipeline`, `domain/workflow-engine`.

## Feature MVC (`features/<entity>-<objective>/`)

Feature folders are **operator jobs**, not entity dumps. Noun-first: `brand-browse`, `tenant-create`, `build-step-workspace`.

```text
features/{entity}-{objective}/
  models/              Zod for this job only
  views/pages/         one page (or none if the route composes)
  views/components/    presentational TSX
  views/phases/<phase>/ optional multi-phase workspace panels
  controllers/         Formik + list controllers
  hooks/               non-form UI hooks
  api/                 TanStack Query for this job
  utilities/           pure helpers — not in views/
  types/               only if not inferable from models
  tests/               Vitest for this job — never `*.test.ts` beside source
  config.ts            optional
  config/              optional (e.g. manifest modules)
```

Omit empty dirs. Shared chrome stays `features/studio-shell`. Shared business rules stay `domain/`. Build lives in `domain/build/pipeline` (one runner for every step) and `domain/build/steps/{step}/tasks/{task}` (code tasks). Deliver send rules live in `domain/deliver` and `features/deliver-send`.

Server actions: `data/<Capability>/`. Thin. Business rules in `domain/`.

## Import law (layers)

Enforced in `eslint.config.mjs` via `eslint-plugin-boundaries` and `import/no-cycle` (**maxDepth 6**). Matches `.cursor/rules/layers.mdc`.

```
feature / app     → data actions, domain, services
data actions      → dpo, dto, dal, domain, services
dpo               → gates, dal, dto
dto               → (pure)
dal               → services/db, drizzle
domain/<entity>   → services, utilities   (NOT data, NOT drizzle, NOT sibling domain)
services          → utilities, data/*/dal, packages/plugins
services/db       → drizzle (pool / migrate / probe only)
```

Domain never drizzle. Services query only via `data/*/dal` except `services/db`.

App/features also import `@eden-ecommerce/design`, `@eden-ecommerce/lib`, and in-repo `@content-studio/plugin-*` / `@content-studio/library-*` (plugins → libraries only; acyclic).

Forbidden: design → app. domain → feature. libraries → plugins. plugins → app. library import cycles. feature → sibling feature **views/pages** or **controllers**. Barrel `index.ts` re-exports. Design/lib root import (`@eden-ecommerce/design` barrel).

`app/(withWrapper)/` routes may **compose** multiple objectives (browse page + create button). Features must not import sibling internals.

Deep imports only. Folder-per-component in design: `{Name}/{Name}`.

PR: correct layer, no forbidden imports, no new barrels, `pnpm lint` passes boundaries.

## Pages

`app/(withWrapper)/` routes thin. Compose feature `views/pages/*`.
Bare galleries / previews use `app/(withoutWrapper)/` (no Studio shell).
